    {
      "name": "an invoked skill with a request says what the request is",
      "input": {
        "op": "renderInvokedSkill",
        "skill": {
          "id": "docx",
          "name": "docx",
          "description": "Creates Word documents."
        },
        "request": "a list"
      },
      "expected": "The user started this message with /docx, which runs the docx skill. Its instructions are loaded under LOADED SKILLS in your instructions, so there is no need to call use_skill for it. The request that came with it: a list"
    },
    {
      "name": "an invoked skill without a request asks what to apply it to",
      "input": {
        "op": "renderInvokedSkill",
        "skill": {
          "id": "Dock-Ops",
          "name": "Dock Ops",
          "description": "Operates docks."
        },
        "request": ""
      },
      "expected": "The user started this message with /Dock-Ops, which runs the Dock Ops skill. Its instructions are loaded under LOADED SKILLS in your instructions, so there is no need to call use_skill for it. It came with no further request, so ask what the user wants it applied to if that is not clear from the conversation."
    },
    {
      "name": "the skill list shows only the skills the model may invoke",
      "input": {
        "op": "describeSkills",
        "skills": [
          {
            "id": "docx",
            "name": "docx",
            "description": "Creates Word documents."
          },
          {
            "id": "code-review",
            "name": "Code review",
            "description": "Reviews code changes.",
            "modelInvocable": false
          },
          {
            "id": "Dock-Ops",
            "name": "Dock Ops",
            "description": "Operates docks."
          }
        ]
      },
      "expected": "SKILLS\n\nSkills are instructions for particular kinds of job, some shipped with Draggy and some written by the user. The description says when each one applies.\n\n- docx: Creates Word documents.\n- Dock-Ops: Dock Ops. Operates docks.\n\nWhen a request matches one, call use_skill with its id before you start, and follow what it says. When none of them matches, work as you normally would and do not mention them."
    },
    {
